<div>
  <h3>Left Aligned (Default)</h3>
  <p class="text-left">
    This paragraph demonstrates left alignment, which is the default for body text in most languages
    that read from left to right. It provides the most natural reading experience.
  </p>

  <h3>Center Aligned</h3>
  <p class="text-center">
    This paragraph demonstrates center alignment, often used for headlines, taglines, or decorative
    text. Use sparingly for body content as it reduces readability.
  </p>

  <h3>Right Aligned</h3>
  <p class="text-right">
    This paragraph demonstrates right alignment, less common in Western languages but useful for
    specific design contexts or languages that read from right to left.
  </p>
</div>
